// The sheet's own notes already flag the mismatch: "pooled/instant heal
// allocation diverges from an aura/HoT -> approximation. Targets up to six
// creatures of choice within range (multi-target, not a contiguous aura)."
// No primitive lets a caster pick specific targets out of a crowd for a
// one-shot heal; `BasicAura`'s `AuraBuffConstructor` only wraps a
// `BuffKind` applied to whoever is in range when the (very short-lived)
// aura entity exists. Ships as the same shape
// `assets/common/abilities/sceptre/healingaura.ron` already uses for an
// "instant party heal": `aura_duration: Some(1.0)` (the aura entity only
// exists for ~1s, so it reads as a single burst rather than a lingering
// field) applying a short `Regeneration` HoT to every ally in range at
// that moment -- not capped at six, and not player-selectable, both
// documented deviations from the sheet's literal "up to six chosen"
// wording.
//
// `AuraBuffConstructor.pool_split` (a shared-pool-divided-among-N-nearest
// mechanic, see common/src/comp/aura.rs) would cap targets at 6 for real,
// but it requires per-class-level scaling config (`unlock_level`,
// `value_at_unlock`, `value_at_max_level`) with no established default for
// a spell that isn't a class-leveled feature -- not used here for that
// reason, same as every other shipped `BasicAura` heal in this asset tree.
BasicAura(
    buildup_duration: 0.2,
    cast_duration: 0.3,
    recover_duration: 0.3,
    targets: InGroup,
    auras: [
        (
            kind: Regeneration,
            strength: 1.0,
            duration: Some(6.0),
        ),
    ],
    aura_duration: Some(1.0),
    range: 18.0,
    energy_cost: 55.0,
    scales_with_combo: false,
    specifier: Some(HealingAura),
    meta: (school: Some(Evocation), source: Some(Divine)),
)
